                                                "example_id": "6fa93c84-bdcb-4ec9-9148-6c044d246dd1",
                                                "sense_id": "7bdca360-ed71-3add-90ce-e19b8cebcb32",
                                                "text": "Holly Near […] interpreter for the deaf Susan Freudlich […] and pianist J. T. Thomas […] appeared in Bostonr Nov. 28 as part of a national tour aimed at educating people about nuclear power. […] The concert was introduced by Dr. Helen Caldicott (left) author of Nuclear Madness and a founder of the anti-nuke movement in Australia."
